            <div xml:id="d609">

                <pb facs="0665" n="653" xml:id="pg653"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.24/723: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-02-26T18:00:00-03:00">February 26, 1942—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 9:38 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>609. For the Under Secretary. Your telegram 276, February 5, 2 p.m. Are all items
                    listed in third paragraph of your message to President Vargas distinct from the
                    items named in paragraph four of the text of Department’s 34 to American
                    delegation, January 19, 10 p.m.? In other words, what specifically has been set
                    aside for or delivered to Brazilian Army, aside from aircraft?</p>
                <p>Also reference Department’s telegram 388, February 18, 9 p.m., please confirm
                    that planes mentioned under number 1 are AT–6[’s].</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
